# =============================================================================
# Line endings
#
# Every script in .devcontainer/ is executed by a POSIX shell - either inside
# the throwaway alpine container that runs initializeCommand (host-bootstrap.sh)
# or by bash inside the devcontainer (post-create / post-start / local-stack).
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true by default, which would check
# these out with CRLF; `sh` then reads the trailing \r as part of every token
# and the script dies on its first line ("set: - invalid option", "syntax
# error: unexpected end of file"), which surfaces as an opaque
# "initializeCommand ... failed" from the devcontainer CLI.
#
# So: normalize to LF in the index AND force LF in the working tree, on every
# OS, regardless of the user's autocrlf setting. Nothing here needs CRLF - the
# consumer of every file in this repo is a Linux container.
#
# After adding/changing this file, an EXISTING Windows checkout still has CRLF
# on disk. Fix it once with:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git checkout -- .
# =============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit for the file types that actually break, so intent survives even
# if the blanket rule above is ever narrowed.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
env.*   text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
